# Scripts that run inside Linux containers must keep LF endings no matter which
# host checked them out. The Dockerfile COPYs docker/entrypoint.sh straight from
# the working tree, so a CRLF checkout on Windows bakes a `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang
# into the image; the kernel cannot resolve that interpreter and every container
# start dies with "exec /entrypoint.sh failed: No such file or directory".
*.sh text eol=lf
